1
00:00:05,260 --> 00:00:07,440
Chuo Ward, Tokyo.

2
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:14,500
The area jutting out from the Sumida River into
Tokyo Port has long been called Tsukudajima.

3
00:00:15,220 --> 00:00:18,700
It sits on the delta where the Sumida
River splits from the Harumi Canal.

4
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:21,920
Originally, as its name suggests,
it was an island,

5
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:24,945
but it was later reclaimed and
joined to Tsukishima in the north

6
00:00:24,995 --> 00:00:27,660
and Ishikawajima in the south.

7
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:32,160
Its official name today is Tsukuda 1-chome.

8
00:00:35,820 --> 00:00:37,740
Tsukudajima has changed quite a bit,
hasn't it.

9
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:40,780
I've read about it in a book, though.

10
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:44,560
This area used to be a ferry landing,
didn't it?

11
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:48,120
That was before Tsukuda Bridge was built.

12
00:00:48,780 --> 00:00:52,020
Ferry boats, like the ones you
always see in period dramas, right?

13
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:55,920
Not quite, but it's more or less the same.

14
00:00:57,660 --> 00:01:03,240
Across to Akashi-chō on the other side, both ends
of Tsukuda Bridge were the private boat landings.

15
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:06,550
A steamboat towed the passenger boats,
and the trip took just four,

16
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:08,060
five minutes.

17
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:10,400
It was free, so we used it all the time.

18
00:01:11,080 --> 00:01:11,480
Really.

19
00:01:12,060 --> 00:01:13,980
That reminds me.

20
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:16,380
See that floodgate over there?

21
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:21,000
There wasn't one back then, so we could
launch boats right onto the Sumida River.

22
00:01:21,620 --> 00:01:25,220
Behind Tsukudajima was the boat landing,
and we used to play there a lot.

23
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,740
I built a raft with Tonpei and Chinkichi,
the three of us.

24
00:01:29,740 --> 00:01:31,760
It was a pretty serious one, you know.

25
00:01:32,580 --> 00:01:34,880
Chinkichi,
watch out for the boat on the right!

26
00:01:35,880 --> 00:01:37,340
It's fine, engine full throttle!

27
00:01:38,460 --> 00:01:41,220
The Sumida River gets pretty busy with traffic,
you know.

28
00:01:41,860 --> 00:01:45,160
When a boat passes, the waves
come all the way up to the landing.

29
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:47,520
The raft gets tossed around violently.

30
00:01:50,760 --> 00:01:52,160
Alright, hang on!

31
00:01:54,180 --> 00:01:55,800
That was fun, wasn't it.

32
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:00,860
N-no way...

33
00:02:00,860 --> 00:02:02,200
What's wrong, Ryo-chan?

34
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:03,780
That Ombrum, you know.

35
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:08,460
Yattokomaru?

36
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:10,120
What a strange name.

37
00:02:11,020 --> 00:02:13,340
Do you remember something, senpai?

38
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:15,160
Yeah.

39
00:02:20,180 --> 00:02:24,120
When you watch TV,
brighten the room and sit back a bit, okay?

40
00:02:33,740 --> 00:02:37,280
Broke folks, come on over to my place.

41
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:42,040
I'm broke too, but don't worry.

42
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:49,040
Hey, look at the blue sky and white clouds.

43
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:55,920
Somehow or other,
it'll all work out eventually.

44
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:12,900
Jobless folks, come on over to my place.

45
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:17,520
I'm jobless too, but don't worry.

46
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:24,540
Look at the steel-gray clouds burning red.

47
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:31,260
Somehow or other,
it'll all work out eventually.

48
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:36,540
You get it, right? Got it, got it.

49
00:03:36,540 --> 00:03:40,460
Once you do, gather up and follow me.

50
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:56,040
Kankichi's Adventure

51
00:03:59,540 --> 00:04:03,040
Back then,
frontier westerns were all the rage,

52
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:06,140
and we went to see one at the Cinerama,
the multi-screen theater.

53
00:04:06,140 --> 00:04:09,660
It was a powerful film,
with three screens joined together.

54
00:04:12,420 --> 00:04:16,760
The scene where they ride a raft down
the rapids was especially intense.

55
00:04:23,620 --> 00:04:28,120
Sitting in the front row,
you'd swear the spray was going to hit you!

56
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:32,800
That was incredible, wasn't it?

57
00:04:33,540 --> 00:04:37,320
Hey, everyone, let's not just
float our raft around Tsukudajima,

58
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:39,980
let's take on a real adventure!

59
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:41,620
An adventure?

60
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:43,940
What are you planning, Kankichi?

61
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:45,920
We're going down the Sumida River!

62
00:04:47,520 --> 00:04:47,780
Blue?

63
00:04:48,820 --> 00:04:52,047
Starting from Senju-Ōhashi,
past Suijin-Ōhashi,

64
00:04:52,097 --> 00:04:53,061
Shirahige Bridge,

65
00:04:53,111 --> 00:04:55,206
Kototoi Bridge, Azuma Bridge,

66
00:04:55,256 --> 00:04:57,402
Komagata Bridge, Umae Bridge,

67
00:04:57,452 --> 00:04:59,952
Kuramae Bridge, Ryōgoku Bridge,

68
00:05:00,002 --> 00:05:03,091
past Kiyosu Bridge and under Eitai Bridge,

69
00:05:03,141 --> 00:05:05,300
all the way down to this Tsukudajima.

70
00:05:05,520 --> 00:05:09,140
Wow, awesome! Sounds like a real adventure!

71
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:10,800
Yeah! Let's do it!

72
00:05:11,700 --> 00:05:13,560
All three of us got really excited.

73
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:16,280
Of course,
you never know what might get in the way,

74
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:17,920
so we kept it a secret from our parents.

75
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:27,540
Thanks, mister.

76
00:05:27,540 --> 00:05:28,420
Thanks.

77
00:05:29,160 --> 00:05:30,320
Be careful.

78
00:05:32,860 --> 00:05:33,760
Well then,

79
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:37,600
here we go!

80
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:48,980
Departing, forward!

81
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:49,980
Alright!

82
00:05:49,980 --> 00:05:51,940
Full speed ahead!

83
00:05:51,940 --> 00:05:53,840
Set course for the Hokuhoku Star!

84
00:05:53,840 --> 00:05:56,180
Which way is the Hokuhoku Star, Kankichi?

85
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:00,860
This way's the opposite direction!

86
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:03,080
Doesn't matter which way!

87
00:06:03,080 --> 00:06:04,680
Don't sweat the small stuff.

88
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:06,640
You'll ruin the mood!

89
00:06:07,180 --> 00:06:07,880
Yeah, you're right.

90
00:06:08,940 --> 00:06:11,560
Now, off on our adventure!

91
00:06:11,840 --> 00:06:12,440
Aye!

92
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:21,380
We're almost at Suijin Bridge

93
00:06:23,500 --> 00:06:25,640
Yeah, once we round this bend.

94
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:32,360
Let's show off to them!

95
00:06:32,820 --> 00:06:34,880
Hey! Hey!

96
00:06:36,660 --> 00:06:37,540
What's that?

97
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:41,460
How about that?
Pretty amazing, right? Hehe, nah-nah!

98
00:06:41,460 --> 00:06:48,020
Aa-bu-yo, spank-spank on the bottom!

99
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:51,480
Thanks, Amora! You'd better remember this!

100
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:55,820
Well then, shall we get going?

101
00:06:57,680 --> 00:06:58,560
Ta-da!

102
00:06:58,560 --> 00:07:01,500
Wow, that's amazing. You brought that?

103
00:07:01,500 --> 00:07:03,560
What did you guys bring?

104
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:05,700
I'm the Igo Submarine.

105
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:08,500
I'm the Antarctic Observation Ship Soya.

106
00:07:08,980 --> 00:07:12,240
Alright, let's flood these guys too!

107
00:07:18,640 --> 00:07:23,480
Yeah, nice, nice!

108
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:26,500
The citrus Yamato really packs a punch,
doesn't it?

109
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:28,120
It looks just like the real thing.

110
00:07:31,540 --> 00:07:34,460
My Antarctic survey ship
Soya isn't bad either!

111
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:36,820
How cool!

112
00:07:41,960 --> 00:07:43,060
That's them!

113
00:07:43,260 --> 00:07:44,240
Hey, you bastards!

114
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:46,980
Okay, full broadside!

115
00:07:51,700 --> 00:07:52,560
Stop it!

116
00:07:54,720 --> 00:07:56,400
Stop it, Otara! You idiot!

117
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:04,480
Alright, we've hit the edge zone.
Retrieve the ships!

118
00:08:05,700 --> 00:08:06,640
Hurry, hurry!

119
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:11,103
Damn it,

120
00:08:11,153 --> 00:08:14,260
One of the 46-centimeter guns is broken.

121
00:08:14,260 --> 00:08:16,140
Mine's radar got knocked out.

122
00:08:16,140 --> 00:08:17,840
All-out attack, it's already today...

123
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:20,180
Come on, get over there!

124
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:30,700
That guy...

125
00:08:31,220 --> 00:08:32,220
did he run away?

126
00:08:34,860 --> 00:08:35,900
The Gamilas!

127
00:08:36,420 --> 00:08:38,200
Yeah! It's a rickety old squid!

128
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:40,280
If you've got guts, come up here!

129
00:08:40,760 --> 00:08:42,220
Shut up! Bring it on!

130
00:08:42,380 --> 00:08:43,440
Go to hell!

131
00:08:47,660 --> 00:08:49,620
Justice always wins.

132
00:08:49,620 --> 00:08:50,740
Hey, Kankichi!

133
00:08:50,740 --> 00:08:51,200
Pole!

134
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:54,480
Sao sao sao

135
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:56,040
Sao sao sao

136
00:08:59,220 --> 00:09:00,380
What do we do?

137
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:03,040
There's nothing that can take my place,
you know.

138
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:04,740
So we're paddling by hand?

139
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:07,320
Kankichi!

140
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:08,880
Full speed! We're gonna crash!

141
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:11,100
Heavy side, all the way!

142
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:13,220
Which one's the heavy side?

143
00:09:15,220 --> 00:09:17,320
Doesn't matter, just dodge!

144
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:19,560
Hello!

145
00:09:29,340 --> 00:09:32,360
There was a compass and a map in there,
you know.

146
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:33,520
Give up already.

147
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:36,120
There's no turning back now.

148
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:38,440
Our supplies disappearing halfway through...

149
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:40,800
It's just like a real adventure, isn't it?

150
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:42,240
But still...

151
00:09:42,240 --> 00:09:51,220
Come on, this is when we have to help each other, that's what makes it an adventure!
Everyone, bring out your things! What, mine's the only stuff left?

152
00:09:52,100 --> 00:10:00,140
Let's see, a water bottle, the chocolate...
and four onigiri. It's all food!

153
00:10:00,620 --> 00:10:07,460
Well, food is important, right? And the toolbox...
a lot of that got washed away too.

154
00:10:07,460 --> 00:10:09,396
Nails and a hammer,

155
00:10:09,446 --> 00:10:12,000
and a small knife. That's it.

156
00:10:16,060 --> 00:10:17,180
That's good!

157
00:10:18,060 --> 00:10:21,600
Tonpei's family runs a sushi shop,
so their rice is just different.

158
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:24,820
Stop it, my family just eats regular rice.

159
00:10:24,820 --> 00:10:27,280
By the way, there's one left.

160
00:10:28,140 --> 00:10:31,280
This is an adventure,
so we've got to share everything.

161
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:33,980
I'll split it three ways.

162
00:10:33,980 --> 00:10:35,180
I'll do it.

163
00:10:36,060 --> 00:10:37,080
It's me.

164
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:37,840
It's me!

165
00:10:37,860 --> 00:10:39,800
Kankichi's bad at math, right!

166
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,600
You're no better!

167
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:43,300
Quit it, you two.

168
00:10:46,060 --> 00:10:47,100
Aaaaah!

169
00:10:50,300 --> 00:10:51,520
Aaaaaah.

170
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:51,640
Aaaaaah.

171
00:10:51,640 --> 00:10:53,020
Eeeeeeh.

172
00:10:58,340 --> 00:10:59,700
Rice balls.

173
00:11:00,380 --> 00:11:02,040
It's not my fault.

174
00:11:02,040 --> 00:11:04,020
Don't be so disappointed.

175
00:11:04,020 --> 00:11:07,700
Doesn't this make it more
like a real adventure?

176
00:11:08,300 --> 00:11:10,660
I can see right through to the other side!

177
00:11:10,660 --> 00:11:12,560
Eeeh!

178
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:14,520
Where are we now?

179
00:11:14,520 --> 00:11:15,515
Right now,

180
00:11:15,565 --> 00:11:18,528
we just passed Kotodoi Bridge,

181
00:11:18,578 --> 00:11:20,520
so we're not even halfway yet.

182
00:11:20,700 --> 00:11:22,160
There's still that much left?

183
00:11:25,940 --> 00:11:28,860
Hey, hey,
don't drink all of that by yourself.

184
00:11:29,260 --> 00:11:31,100
Come on, it's my water!

185
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:32,220
Now it's everyone's water.

186
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:34,140
Don't hog it. Hand it over.

187
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:34,880
No way.

188
00:11:35,060 --> 00:11:36,420
Cut it out, you two.

189
00:11:37,420 --> 00:11:38,260
Cut it out.

190
00:11:49,720 --> 00:11:52,920
I'm starving,
and we only have one rice ball.

191
00:11:56,460 --> 00:12:00,400
And we're saving the
chocolate bar for emergencies.

192
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:02,720
So what counts as an emergency?

193
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:04,940
Like right now, obviously.

194
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:09,440
Every adventure has moments like this.

195
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:16,340
We should've brought fishing gear.

196
00:12:16,940 --> 00:12:19,500
I've got a knife,
so I could gut the fish for you.

197
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:21,600
Fish or chocolate, either one would be good.

198
00:12:21,600 --> 00:12:24,700
Don't say that. I'll only want it more.

199
00:12:27,400 --> 00:12:28,920
What are you doing, Kankichi?

200
00:12:29,520 --> 00:12:31,200
I'm going to dive down and catch some fish.

201
00:12:32,340 --> 00:12:35,300
In an adventure,
you have to do everything yourself.

202
00:12:35,300 --> 00:12:37,500
Kankichi, are you serious?

203
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:40,040
Don't underestimate me.

204
00:12:40,820 --> 00:12:41,800
I'm fine.

205
00:12:43,340 --> 00:12:44,280
Just a kid.

206
00:12:45,380 --> 00:12:47,040
He actually jumped in!

207
00:12:52,140 --> 00:12:53,740
He still hasn't come up

208
00:12:55,360 --> 00:12:57,140
Isn't he gone a bit too long?

209
00:12:58,200 --> 00:12:59,000
Yeah, he is.

210
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:01,180
Kankichi!

211
00:13:01,180 --> 00:13:01,860
Cheers!

212
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:03,780
Gakiji!

213
00:13:05,860 --> 00:13:07,140
Whoa, it's huge.

214
00:13:08,820 --> 00:13:10,900
I've never seen an eel this big.

215
00:13:10,900 --> 00:13:13,180
Yeah, it might be the river's guardian.

216
00:13:16,580 --> 00:13:19,740
If we grilled it, we'd probably be punished.

217
00:13:19,740 --> 00:13:20,760
Yeah.

218
00:13:21,420 --> 00:13:23,060
Let's just put it back
in the river after all.

219
00:13:23,420 --> 00:13:24,220
That sounds good.

220
00:13:26,640 --> 00:13:27,620
Take care, okay?

221
00:13:28,180 --> 00:13:30,900
Let's meet again when we're grown up.

222
00:13:36,180 --> 00:13:37,460
Let's eat the chocolate bar.

223
00:13:37,460 --> 00:13:40,540
But you were saving it for every day, right?

224
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:43,520
Now is the every day.

225
00:13:44,340 --> 00:13:45,080
I see.

226
00:13:45,680 --> 00:13:46,640
Yeah, that's right.

227
00:14:05,620 --> 00:14:10,260
Ugh, even the emergency
chocolate bar is so tiny.

228
00:14:10,860 --> 00:14:12,240
I'm thirsty too.

229
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:16,100
I'd kill for some anpan
and ramune right now.

230
00:14:19,880 --> 00:14:21,080
Let's just quit already.

231
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:24,760
What? Quitting the Tonpe? That's not fair.

232
00:14:25,160 --> 00:14:28,440
I'm already sick of it, and I'm starving.

233
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:33,020
We decided this ourselves. An adventure means
nothing unless you see it through to the end.

234
00:14:33,020 --> 00:14:35,140
There's meaning in quitting too, you know.

235
00:14:35,620 --> 00:14:37,960
What did you say?
Say that again! You're out!

236
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:39,420
What?!

237
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:40,500
Stop it, you two!

238
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:43,300
We always settle things by majority
vote in situations like this!

239
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:45,860
Yeah! Let's decide it by majority vote!

240
00:14:46,140 --> 00:14:47,500
Anyone who wants to quit here,
raise your hand!

241
00:14:49,020 --> 00:14:50,980
Anyone who wants to keep going to the end,
raise your hand!

242
00:14:52,800 --> 00:14:54,580
So which way is the majority?

243
00:14:54,880 --> 00:14:56,060
We're seeing this through to the end, right!

244
00:14:56,900 --> 00:14:57,900
Yeah...

245
00:14:58,280 --> 00:15:01,700
We set out on an adventure,
so quitting halfway through would be...

246
00:15:01,700 --> 00:15:02,660
Look, look!

247
00:15:03,780 --> 00:15:04,500
But...

248
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:04,960
But what?

249
00:15:05,860 --> 00:15:08,380
It's too slow, so it's boring.

250
00:15:08,380 --> 00:15:11,620
If only there were a way to go faster.

251
00:15:11,620 --> 00:15:15,300
Even if you say that,
it's not like it has an engine, you know.

252
00:15:15,300 --> 00:15:17,780
We've got no choice but
to go with the flow, right?

253
00:15:22,900 --> 00:15:24,440
I've got a great idea!

254
00:15:28,880 --> 00:15:30,420
What's with this pile of trash?

255
00:15:30,420 --> 00:15:31,660
What are we gonna do with all this stuff?

256
00:15:31,660 --> 00:15:33,220
We're gonna make one.

257
00:15:33,220 --> 00:15:35,380
Kankichi's place is a lantern shop, right?

258
00:15:35,620 --> 00:15:38,280
We're gonna paste layers
of that newspaper together.

259
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:40,400
I get it, but we'll need nori.

260
00:15:40,880 --> 00:15:42,800
We've got these squashed rice balls.

261
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:43,720
I see.

262
00:15:49,940 --> 00:15:50,340
Done!

263
00:16:07,220 --> 00:16:08,300
Yes!

264
00:16:09,680 --> 00:16:10,920
That's Kiyosu Bridge!

265
00:16:11,740 --> 00:16:13,600
Once we pass under Edo Bridge,

266
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:15,120
Tsukudajima is just ahead!

267
00:16:23,240 --> 00:16:25,500
The sky's looking suspicious.

268
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:27,540
Looks like we're in for some rain.

269
00:16:28,420 --> 00:16:29,020
Here it comes!

270
00:16:38,760 --> 00:16:39,900
What do we do now?

271
00:16:39,900 --> 00:16:40,740
Kawakichi!

272
00:16:48,980 --> 00:16:51,440
Hold on tight so you don't fall off!

273
00:16:54,440 --> 00:16:55,320
Whoa!

274
00:16:56,620 --> 00:16:59,060
Kawaguchi! That was Heitai Bridge!

275
00:16:59,160 --> 00:16:59,320
What?!

276
00:17:02,140 --> 00:17:03,080
That means -

277
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:05,300
Fukudajima is to the right!

278
00:17:07,020 --> 00:17:09,900
No good!
The wind is so strong, it won't move at all!

279
00:17:10,320 --> 00:17:11,600
W-wait, the wind!

280
00:17:17,380 --> 00:17:18,900
No! We won't make it in time!

281
00:17:19,620 --> 00:17:20,460
We're going to crash!

282
00:17:25,760 --> 00:17:27,300
Oh no! My Yamato!

283
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:55,920
Rough waters! At this rate, we'll go down!

284
00:17:56,180 --> 00:17:56,960
Whoa!

285
00:18:17,460 --> 00:18:20,220
Ugh, it's getting cold.

286
00:18:20,220 --> 00:18:23,760
I wonder which way the land is.

287
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:25,480
Well...

288
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:31,080
Hey, let's huddle closer.

289
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:36,700
Damn, it's turned into a storm!

290
00:18:37,220 --> 00:18:39,880
The weather forecast didn't
say a thing about this!

291
00:18:42,900 --> 00:18:43,720
Sorry.

292
00:18:44,940 --> 00:18:48,080
What are you talking about?
Thanks to you, we had a great adventure!

293
00:18:48,600 --> 00:18:50,640
Yeah, you don't have to apologize.

294
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:52,880
This raft was doing 60 kilometers an hour!

295
00:18:54,220 --> 00:18:58,640
Yeah, it was way faster than the gardener's truck,
wasn't it?

296
00:19:05,180 --> 00:19:09,320
When I get married and have a kid,
I'm gonna talk to this one.

297
00:19:10,080 --> 00:19:11,980
Getting married means
you need a partner, right?

298
00:19:11,980 --> 00:19:14,900
Who is it? Who do you like, Chinkichi?

299
00:19:14,900 --> 00:19:17,620
Got it, mine's the cute one, right?

300
00:19:18,820 --> 00:19:20,960
I don't want to be the only one who tells.

301
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:23,760
Then let's all say it together on three.

302
00:19:23,760 --> 00:19:26,300
This is a secret just
between the three of us, okay?

303
00:19:26,300 --> 00:19:27,720
Alright, pinky swear.

304
00:19:29,520 --> 00:19:34,920
Pinky swear, a thousand needles if we lie.

305
00:19:35,500 --> 00:19:39,100
But seriously,
swallowing a thousand needles would be awful

306
00:19:39,100 --> 00:19:39,840
Could anyone swallow that?

307
00:19:39,840 --> 00:19:43,340
Who cares about that?
We're talking about the girl you like.

308
00:19:43,340 --> 00:19:46,220
Then let's say it. Ready, go.

309
00:19:46,220 --> 00:19:48,480
Momoyo-chan from Class 3.

310
00:19:50,500 --> 00:19:52,260
Geez, you're all the same, aren't you?

311
00:19:52,860 --> 00:19:55,520
Well, she's cute, right?
And she's so gentle.

312
00:19:56,300 --> 00:19:58,660
But, you know,
Momoyo-chan's a rich young lady.

313
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:00,940
Would someone like us
even be marriage material?

314
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:02,180
Idiot.

315
00:20:02,180 --> 00:20:04,700
Sure, we're like this right now,

316
00:20:04,700 --> 00:20:08,200
but who knows how important
we'll be once we grow up.

317
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:08,920
I see.

318
00:20:08,920 --> 00:20:11,780
I might become a space pilot.

319
00:20:12,280 --> 00:20:14,320
Me, I just want to be rich.

320
00:20:14,320 --> 00:20:16,900
I'm the captain of the Earth Defense Force.

321
00:20:16,900 --> 00:20:18,280
As if that'd ever happen.

322
00:20:19,740 --> 00:20:20,620
And then, you know,

323
00:20:20,620 --> 00:20:24,060
Momoyo-chan will be the
one begging us to marry her.

324
00:20:29,440 --> 00:20:31,280
A boat! It's coming this way!

325
00:20:32,180 --> 00:20:33,500
Hey! Hey!

326
00:20:34,320 --> 00:20:35,200
Yoo-hoo!

327
00:20:36,260 --> 00:20:37,100
Yoo-hoo!

328
00:20:38,220 --> 00:20:42,220
H-hey,

329
00:20:43,680 --> 00:20:45,680
they don't seem to notice us.

330
00:20:45,680 --> 00:20:49,260
Hey! Oh no! We've got to dodge!

331
00:20:49,680 --> 00:20:58,640
Damn it!

332
00:20:59,440 --> 00:20:59,900
Gah!

333
00:20:59,980 --> 00:21:01,020
Ugh!

334
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:04,840
Kankichi!

335
00:21:06,100 --> 00:21:07,100
Kankichi!

336
00:21:10,740 --> 00:21:11,400
Whoa!

337
00:21:14,940 --> 00:21:16,760
I thought I was going to die...

338
00:21:16,760 --> 00:21:17,580
Kankichi!

339
00:21:17,780 --> 00:21:18,980
Thank goodness...

340
00:21:18,980 --> 00:21:19,980
Tonpe!

341
00:21:20,140 --> 00:21:20,820
Kankichi!

342
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:21,840
Thank goodness!

343
00:21:22,060 --> 00:21:22,940
You're safe!

344
00:21:23,020 --> 00:21:23,740
Ugh!

345
00:21:31,520 --> 00:21:33,820
Got rammed into...

346
00:21:34,480 --> 00:21:34,920
me

347
00:21:37,760 --> 00:21:41,380
me Whatever was stuck on
the fish's face came off!

348
00:21:41,380 --> 00:21:41,940
me

349
00:21:46,620 --> 00:21:53,260
That's the boat, you see...
well, it was decades ago, so

350
00:21:53,260 --> 00:21:55,620
That old man might be dead by now, too.

351
00:22:00,340 --> 00:22:02,700
It's a ghost! A ghost!

352
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:05,960
Something like that, I guess.

353
00:22:05,960 --> 00:22:07,160
Heh heh heh.

354
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:10,380
What ghost?! I'm alive!

355
00:22:10,440 --> 00:22:14,520
Really? But you haven't
changed at all since back then!

356
00:22:15,660 --> 00:22:17,920
Hahahahahaha!

357
00:22:17,920 --> 00:22:21,320
So, you're the brat from back then

358
00:22:23,260 --> 00:22:25,040
How old are you anyway?

359
00:22:25,040 --> 00:22:27,960
I've been an old man for,
what, thirty or forty years now.

360
00:22:27,960 --> 00:22:29,180
I've been an old man for,
what, thirty or forty years now.

361
00:22:29,180 --> 00:22:31,740
It's great to see you're doing well.

362
00:22:31,740 --> 00:22:33,720
Still, what a coincidence.

363
00:22:33,720 --> 00:22:34,800
Yes, indeed.

364
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:38,080
After that,
I found something in the sea, you know.

365
00:22:38,080 --> 00:22:41,320
It's mine.

366
00:22:41,320 --> 00:22:43,800
It's my Yamato that I lost back then.

367
00:22:43,800 --> 00:22:44,780
Riza?

368
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:46,640
I'm glad, Senpai.

369
00:22:46,640 --> 00:22:47,480
Really.

370
00:22:48,040 --> 00:22:49,420
My Yamato.

371
00:22:49,420 --> 00:22:52,080
Yeah, no doubt about it. This is it.

372
00:22:55,440 --> 00:22:57,420
Good, good, engine off.

373
00:22:59,280 --> 00:23:01,680
I could die happy.

374
00:23:02,760 --> 00:23:05,780
Sometimes I envy Ryo-chan like that.

375
00:23:05,780 --> 00:23:06,820
Really, it is.

376
00:23:06,820 --> 00:23:10,200
At this rate, he'll live a long time.

377
00:23:10,200 --> 00:23:10,640
(laughter)

378
00:23:12,340 --> 00:23:13,420
(laughter)

379
00:23:13,420 --> 00:23:13,560
(laughter)

380
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:13,980
(laughter)

381
00:23:13,980 --> 00:23:14,620
(laughter)

382
00:23:14,620 --> 00:23:14,740
(laughter)

383
00:23:14,740 --> 00:23:16,100
(laughter)

384
00:23:16,100 --> 00:23:16,200
(laughter)

385
00:23:16,200 --> 00:23:16,480
(laughter)

386
00:23:16,480 --> 00:23:18,400
(laughter)

387
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:19,180
(laughter)

388
00:23:19,180 --> 00:23:20,140
(laughter)

389
00:23:20,140 --> 00:23:21,020
Haha, yeah.

390
00:24:19,880 --> 00:24:27,340
I probably don't want to be someone
who plays dumb games based on looks.

391
00:24:27,340 --> 00:24:34,320
If I dawdle at the street corner,
the moon slips away.

392
00:24:34,320 --> 00:24:42,500
Now isn't everything,
so don't get too worked up.

393
00:24:42,500 --> 00:24:46,240
Even if you fib a little and cheat a little,

394
00:24:46,240 --> 00:24:50,400
sometimes while you're helping someone.

395
00:24:50,400 --> 00:24:53,410
Baby, do you know me?

396
00:24:53,460 --> 00:24:54,480
Toward tomorrow.

397
00:24:54,480 --> 00:24:56,660
What a nice spirit!

398
00:24:57,920 --> 00:25:01,760
I won't rot away, I'll do what needs doing.

399
00:25:01,760 --> 00:25:04,220
What a cute spirit!

400
00:25:04,220 --> 00:25:07,620
What's hard to understand is

401
00:25:08,720 --> 00:25:11,700
the image we want to project.

402
00:25:12,900 --> 00:25:17,360
Better than a makeover, right?

403
00:25:19,020 --> 00:25:24,800
Na-na-na-na, na-na-na-na, na-na-na-na...

404
00:25:31,860 --> 00:25:34,060
Hey, this is bad!

405
00:25:34,060 --> 00:25:36,580
I can't stop hiccupping!

406
00:25:36,580 --> 00:25:39,740
At this rate, my life is in danger!

407
00:25:39,740 --> 00:25:42,080
Someone, make it stop!

408
00:25:43,100 --> 00:25:46,560
Next time: Hiccup Panic. See you then!

409
00:25:56,020 --> 00:25:59,240
Everyone, come visit our town!

410
00:26:00,120 --> 00:26:00,800
Thank you!

